{#
Generated by: Claude Code CLI
Date time: 2026/09/09 17:30 SAST
Version: 0.7
Description:
  The course catalogue, browsed by category.

  This page is the taxonomy. It does not list the whole catalogue underneath it: a wall of every
  published course below the categories tells a reader nothing the categories were not already
  telling them, and on a real catalogue it is thousands of cards nobody scrolls.

  The one exception is a search. Somebody who types a course title has asked for courses, and the
  tree cannot answer that, so results replace the tree until the search is cleared.

  Categories are accordions. A chip rail can only offer one level, so a three-level taxonomy
  arrived as a flat row that said nothing about what contained what. The accordions carry the
  shape: a category holds the courses filed directly in it, and its sub-categories are accordions
  inside it. Only a branch that holds a course is here - an empty category, however many
  sub-categories it has, is still empty, and keeping a non-empty branch keeps all of its ancestors.

  Tags are not on this page. There is one tag cloud and it is on the tag page.

  Comments here are plain prose only: no angle brackets, no comment delimiters, no template tokens
  and no code. Each of those is read as markup rather than as text.
Changelog:
  2026/09/09 17:30 SAST
  - Became the categories page: the flat course grid and the tag facets were removed, the duplicated inline course card was replaced by the shared partial, and the course search now returns cards.
  2026/09/07 01:45 SAST
  - The rails became facets: each option carries the number of courses choosing it would return.
#}
{% extends layout %}
{% block page_body %}
	{% set ph_kicker = 'Course catalogue' %}
	{% set ph_title = browse_category ? browse_category.name : 'Browse by category' %}
	{% set ph_lead = browse_category ? (browse_category.description ?: 'Every course in this part of the catalogue, including the levels beneath it.') : 'Open a category to see the courses in it and the categories beneath it.' %}
	{% set ph_action_href = '/courses/tags' %}
	{% set ph_action_label = 'Browse by tag' %}
	{% include '@platform/partials/page-head.html.twig' %}
	<section class="container-fluid cl-container-wide py-4">
		{% if browse_trail %}
			<nav class="cl-breadcrumb" aria-label="Category">
				<a href="/courses">All courses</a>
				{% for crumb in browse_trail %}
					<span class="cl-breadcrumb-sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
					<a href="/courses/category/{{ crumb.slug }}" {% if crumb.slug == browse_category.slug %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ crumb.name }}</a>
				{% endfor %}
			</nav>
		{% endif %}
		{% include '@platform/partials/dataset-search.html.twig' with {ds_name: 'catalogue', ds_label: 'Search courses', ds_value: catalogue_search, ds_action: catalogue_pagination.base} %}
		<div id="catalogue-region" data-server-search-target>
			<div id="catalogue-results">
				{% if searching %}
					{% include '@platform/partials/pagination.html.twig' with {pg: catalogue_pagination} %}
					{% if courses %}
						<div class="cl-course-cards section">
							{% for course in courses %}
								{% include '@platform/partials/course-card.html.twig' with {course: course} %}
							{% endfor %}
						</div>
					{% else %}
						<div class="empty section">
							<h3>
								No course matches that search
							</h3>
						</div>
					{% endif %}
					{% include '@platform/partials/pagination.html.twig' with {pg: catalogue_pagination} %}
				{% elseif category_tree %}
					<div class="cl-category-tree section">
						{% for node in category_tree %}
							{% include '@platform/partials/category-branch.html.twig' with {node: node, depth: 0} %}
						{% endfor %}
					</div>
				{% else %}
					<div class="empty section">
						<h3>
							No categories hold a published course yet
						</h3>
					</div>
				{% endif %}
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
{% endblock %}
